# Windows scripts and the plain-text files that ship beside them must reach a
# Windows machine with CRLF endings, whatever the contributor's platform does
# locally. cmd.exe is unforgiving about this and the files are downloaded, not
# cloned, by the people who run them.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.txt text eol=crlf

*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
